    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "## About\r\n\r\n`MiniGitCommandSplit` is not triggered for `:Git commit` or `:Git rebase`.\r\n\r\nI understand that `MiniGitCommandSplit` fires when the command has completed, so it makes sense that it doesn’t trigger while the command is still in progress. However, for these commands, the name of the event might be a bit misleading.\r\n\r\nPerhaps for commands like these, it should fire once they are displayed in the tab, or it might make sense to introduce a separate event, such as `MiniGitCommandSplitInit`. That said, the only use case I see for such behavior at the moment is adjusting the tab positions for these commands.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h2 dir=\"auto\">About</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><code class=\"notranslate\">MiniGitCommandSplit</code> is not triggered for <code class=\"notranslate\">:Git commit</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">:Git rebase</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I understand that <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniGitCommandSplit</code> fires when the command has completed, so it makes sense that it doesn’t trigger while the command is still in progress. However, for these commands, the name of the event might be a bit misleading.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Perhaps for commands like these, it should fire once they are displayed in the tab, or it might make sense to introduce a separate event, such as <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniGitCommandSplitInit</code>. That said, the only use case I see for such behavior at the moment is adjusting the tab positions for these commands.</p>",
    "bodyText": "About\nMiniGitCommandSplit is not triggered for :Git commit or :Git rebase.\nI understand that MiniGitCommandSplit fires when the command has completed, so it makes sense that it doesn’t trigger while the command is still in progress. However, for these commands, the name of the event might be a bit misleading.\nPerhaps for commands like these, it should fire once they are displayed in the tab, or it might make sense to introduce a separate event, such as MiniGitCommandSplitInit. That said, the only use case I see for such behavior at the moment is adjusting the tab positions for these commands.",
